TO DO for Rtl66 0.2
Chris Ahlstrom
2019-04-13 to 2026-01-06

For version 0.3:

    -   Get one of the Windows APIs to work.
    -   Add a test app to record one track, write it to a
        file, read the file, and play it.

Fixes:

    -   Under JACK:
        -   The nanoKey2 inputs might be spurious.
        -   Playback can yield "jack_process_in() message overflow".
    -   Reconsider deriving bus_in/out from rtmidi_in/out instead
        of membership.
    -   The midiprobe app misleading shows only ALSA as "Compiled APIs".
    -   Fix: midiclock cannot handle "all ports" option.
    -   Fix:
        If JACK is running, the --alsa option leads to the API
        being unspecified.
    -   Need an option in masterbus::choose_port() to show the "All Ports"
        options.
    -   In busout, the port count adds the midi::bus ports, which have
        the app client-name as the clientname part of the port-name.
        Get the I/O port-count before makebus() is called.
    -   Add in/out boolean to rtmidi::get_port_count(), and
        also to an overload that ignoressss
    -   Error in ALSA with play and busout:
       [3] Skip in ALSA buss FLUID Synth (3654322) #0 Caps: W SubW
        play: seq.c:4019: snd_seq_get_queue_tempo: Assertion
        seq && tempo failed.
    -   Need a way to indicate that a MIDI API object *is* for
        the master, and not just *has* a master.
    -   Investigate how RtMidi uses the "reuse connection" concept.
    -   In busin, showing to_string() for masterbus says the main port
        is capture, but the aliases are playback, and vice versa!
    -   Why is not ALSA showing a nickname?
    -   In the bus hierarchy, sort out the engine midi-API vs. the
        bus-specific midi-API.
        -   Polling.
            -   Poll for all ports via the masterbus.
            -   Poll for each port using its own midi_api port and
                jack-process.
    -   Why is the note off always at time 0?

        [cbmidiin] Msg:  3 bytes @ 3285302:  0x90 0x41 0x43 buss/index 255
        [cbmidiin] Msg:  3 bytes @ 0:  0x80 0x41 0x40 buss/index 255

    -   Track down the "uninitialized semaphores" in JACK.
    -   Why does JACK detection when JACK is not running take
        so long?
    -   The midiprobeex does not fall back to ALSA, it just fails.
    -   Fix busin functionality and get_message(). DONE.
        -   The event type includes codes for note on/off and other
            specific events; we should take advantage of this.
    -   Make sure meaningful JACK device aliases can be found.
    -   A sporadic race condition in JACK playback.
    -   play does not reload the PPQN (and BPM?) for each file.
    -   midiprobeex doubles the number of ports.
    -   In create_track(), use the initial track number as a parameter.
    -   In event::append_meta_data(), the message is actually cleared
        before appending. Rename the function or add a bool 'clear' flag.
    -   Make sure trackdata::parse() sets track number correctly.
    -   Update rterror to print the client-tag in error messages.
    -   Investigate differences between behavior of cbmidiin and qmidiin.
    -   In cfg, how about a convention where, instead of just

            --callback      -c

        we have stuff like

            --&callback     which provides -c
            --call&back     which provides -b
            --&call&back    which provides -cb

